\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the Heston PDF obtained via the frFFT method (red line) and the Monte Carlo estimator (blue histogram) for four sample trajectories. }}{63}{figure.6.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the frFFT-recovered density (red dashed) and the analytical Gaussian (blue) for four randomly sampled trajectories. The two curves are visually indistinguishable, confirming the distributional identity established by the zero-distance metrics in Table~\ref {tab:step_c}.}}{68}{figure.6.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Pointwise residuals between the normalised frFFT density and the analytical Gaussian density, evaluated at the active fine-grid points within $\pm 5\sigma $ of each trajectory's mean. The vertical axes carry exponents of $1^{-15}$, confirming that the residuals are at the level of double-precision machine epsilon.}}{69}{figure.6.3}%
